  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "As we all know, throwing on index sucks. Without it being on a physical button, the exact release point is very difficult to predict. My suggestion is that if a pickup does not have any onpickupusedown/up triggers, you should be able to use your trigger to hold/release it. Releasing with an index finger is just so much more natural and it feels great. It is already possible to do the releasing with an onpickupuseup trigger, and this works remarkably well. Check out this world to try it for yourself: https://vrchat.com/home/launch?worldId=wrld_d1c35e61-82e2-4460-ae33-3325d609f361&instanceId=39417~hidden(usr_f74ae803-ad2d-4db2-9b89-367642ba7d5f)~nonce(a306c266-2cc0-4b8b-9a48-e3d170db2d2e)\n\nI think this works so well that it should be made a standard feature everywhere, so that world creators don't have to implement it themselves. And besides, if they did, this particular workaround will break throwing on desktop so it really needs official support",
